<p>European Union lawmakers have again paused work on ratifying a trade deal with the United States, saying they need clarity on how President Trump’s newly announced 15% global import tariff would interact with the agreement. The pause follows a U.S. Supreme Court ruling that struck down many of the President’s earlier tariff actions. After that decision, the White House signaled it would pursue a new 15% tariff using a different legal route. EU officials say they are not scrapping the deal. They want Washington to spell out how it plans to stick to what was agreed, because adding a blanket tariff on top of existing duties could push effective rates above the deal’s intended ceiling. For readers outside Europe and the U.S., the key point is that the two sides are still talking—but businesses may face a short stretch of uncertainty until the tariff rules are clearly laid out.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/cKl4k75twyRvvpOz_i7Odbhy5YeVe1gpWvjkPUEzZZ91aiDvMi74pVo_LaTxg_3b12MOhvvOvrBF-JSLx6HvIH-SvXfpP_B8o4gviOz1TIva1O974NB1w2k4Im0y53UuNDSvWwugTz2VGiveb2mq2FH0q1N22rXNdVVm49AEzt7uUY4q8ALIu3Q4H99LtTngNLEVcXBmZ2DWpu44XC5fLh4bEzuQ0pNUINHqMPeJalaOcfFBwxJc3pKNalyg9enqKzdM9kFQfz8yEYUp5g' alt='A cargo ship loaded with shipping containers at the Port of Oakland amid tariff tensions.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Committee delay: The European Parliament’s trade committee postponed its ratification vote. Chair Bernd Lange said lawmakers need a clear explanation of how the new blanket U.S. tariff policy would fit under the agreement’s negotiated ceiling.</li><li>Legal pathway: Reporting says the White House is leaning on Section 122 authority as the legal hook for an across-the-board import tariff, instead of the earlier approach the courts challenged.</li><li>Political friction: EU lawmakers had already paused work on the trade deal last month. The Hindu reports the earlier halt came amid objections tied to President Trump’s stated desire to acquire Greenland.</li><li>Everyday goods: The dispute could mean higher prices for some consumer products. One European lawmaker pointed to cheeses such as Parmesan and Camembert, which could face tariff rates nearing 30% if duties rise further.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>European Commission: Commission spokesman Olof Gill said the EU sees the agreement as binding and wants the U.S. to clearly show how it will honor it as tariff policy shifts. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/eu-hits-pause-on-us-trade-deal-as-it-seeks-clarity/'>Michael West Media</a>)</li><li>European Parliament trade committee: Chair Bernd Lange said that if Washington adds a new blanket import tariff on top of existing duties, it could break the agreement’s tariff ceiling—so lawmakers are delaying their vote. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/eu-pauses-u-s-trade-deal-as-it-seeks-clarity-over-trumps-new-15-global-tariffs'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>White House (tariff strategy): The administration is looking for another legal basis to keep broad tariffs in place after the Supreme Court invalidated many earlier measures. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/2/23/trumps-new-tariff-threats-trigger-economic-uncertainty-trade-deals-stall'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/23/world/europe/eu-us-trade-deal-pause-tariffs.html'>The European Union Hits Pause on Its U.S. Trade Deal</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/eu-puts-key-us-trade-deal-on-hold-after-supreme-court-ruling-11127101#publisher=newsstand'>EU Puts Key US Trade Deal On Hold After Supreme Court Ruling</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/eu-freezes-us-trade-deal-after-supreme-court-tariff-ruling/a-76095257'>EU freezes US trade deal after Supreme Court tariff ruling</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/european-union-lawmakers-again-postpone-vote-on-us-trade-deal-after-tariff-upheaval/articl